### ###########################################################
###
###  Shift Scheduler — API checks
###
###  Run top to bottom, after:
###      docker compose down -v
###      docker compose up -d      (wait for healthy)
###
###  Schedule lifecycle: COLLECTING -> DRAFT -> PUBLISHED
###      COLLECTING  employees submit constraints, no assignment
###      DRAFT       submission closed, the manager assigns
###      PUBLISHED   planning is done, manual assignment still allowed
###
###  IMPORTANT — version numbers
###  Every change to a schedule raises its version. Requests that lock,
###  publish or edit requirements must send the current one. The numbers
###  below are what a clean run produces; if a request returns
###  "The schedule was changed by someone else", read the version from
###  the previous response and use that.
###
### ###########################################################


### ===========================================================
### 1 — NO SESSION
### ===========================================================

### 1.1 Health check — expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### 1.2 Current user without a session — expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### 1.3 Wrong password — expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123X"}

### 1.4 Disabled account — expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "avi", "password": "password123"}


### ===========================================================
### 2 — MANAGER: SETUP
### ===========================================================

### 2.0 Log in as manager — expect 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123"}

### 2.1 Current user — expect 200, role MANAGER
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me


### ----- 2.2 JOB POSITIONS -----

### 2.2.1 List — expect 200, three positions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions

### 2.2.2 Create — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Team lead"}

### 2.2.3 Duplicate name — expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Support agent"}

### 2.2.4 Empty name — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": ""}

### 2.2.5 Delete a position in use — expect 409
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions/1

### 2.2.6 Unknown id — expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions/999


