### 2.3.1 List — expect 200, Night has crossesMidnight true and 8 hours
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types

### 2.3.2 Create one crossing midnight — expect 201, durationHours 8
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Late night", "startTime": "22:00", "endTime": "06:00"}

### 2.3.3 Same start and end — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Broken", "startTime": "08:00", "endTime": "08:00"}


### ----- 2.4 EMPLOYEES -----

### 2.4.1 List — expect 200, ten employees
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### 2.4.2 Create — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Roni Katz", "username": "roni", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.4.3 Duplicate username — expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Fake", "username": "maya", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.4.4 Unknown job position — expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Ghost", "username": "ghost", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 999}

### 2.4.5 Password too short — expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Short", "username": "shorty", "password": "123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}


### ----- 2.5 OPTIMISTIC LOCKING ON AN EMPLOYEE -----
### A PUT carries every field, so an update built on a stale copy would
### write back the values as they were when the form was opened.

### 2.5.1 Read Maya — expect 200, version 0
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3

### 2.5.2 Manager A changes her hours to 32, sending version 0
###       expect 200, version becomes 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Maya Cohen", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 32, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.3 Manager B still holds version 0 and only meant to fix the name
###       expect 409 — without the check this would restore 40 hours
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Maya Cohen-Levi", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.4 Reload — expect 200, version 1 and 32 hours
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3

### 2.5.5 Retry with version 1, keeping the 32 hours — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 1, "fullName": "Maya Cohen", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 32, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 2}

### 2.5.6 Put her back to 40 for the rest of the run — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 2, "fullName": "Maya Cohen", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 2}


### ----- 2.6 THE LAST MANAGER CANNOT BE REMOVED -----
### Dana is the only manager. Both routes out are guarded, and the count
### is read under a write lock so two concurrent demotions cannot both pass.

### 2.6.1 Deactivate her — expect 400
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1

### 2.6.2 Read Dana — expect 200, note the version
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1

### 2.6.3 Demote her to EMPLOYEE — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Dana Levi", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.4 Set her inactive through update — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Dana Levi", "role": "MANAGER",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": false, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.5 Promote Yoni — expect 200, now there are two managers
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Yoni Barak", "role": "MANAGER",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.6 Now Dana can be demoted — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "fullName": "Dana Levi", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.7 And Yoni, now the only one, cannot — expect 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 1, "fullName": "Yoni Barak", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.8 Dana is an employee now, so restoring her needs Yoni's session
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "yoni", "password": "password123"}

### 2.6.9 Restore Dana as manager — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 1, "fullName": "Dana Levi", "role": "MANAGER",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.10 Demote Yoni back — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 1, "fullName": "Yoni Barak", "role": "EMPLOYEE",
  "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "active": true, "jobPositionId": 1}

### 2.6.11 Back to Dana's session
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123"}


### ----- 2.7 LEAVES -----

### 2.7.1 Omer on leave 10-12 Aug — expect 201, one range of 3 days
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
