### ----- 4.8 EVERYTHING A MANAGER DOES IS REFUSED -----

### 4.8.1 List employees — expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### 4.8.2 Create a job position — expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Hacker"}

### 4.8.3 List leaves — expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves

### 4.8.4 Lock the schedule — expect 403
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/lock
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 2}

### 4.8.5 Assign someone — expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 6, "employeeId": 3, "override": false}


### ===========================================================
### 5 — CLOSING SUBMISSION (COLLECTING -> DRAFT)
### ===========================================================

### 5.0 Back to the manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123"}

### 5.1 Lock with a stale version — expect 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/lock
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0}

### 5.2 Lock with the current version 2 — expect 200, status DRAFT
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/lock
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 2}

### 5.3 Lock again — expect 409, it is no longer COLLECTING
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/lock
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 3}

### 5.4 The manager can still correct a constraint — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 8, "type": "CANNOT", "reason": "Entered by the manager", "employeeId": 5}


### ===========================================================
### 6 — EMPLOYEE, AFTER SUBMISSION CLOSED
### ===========================================================

### 6.0 Log in as maya
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "maya", "password": "password123"}

### 6.1 My week — expect 200, submissionOpen false
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/my-week

### 6.2 Submit a new constraint — expect 409, the window is closed
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 9, "type": "CANNOT"}

### 6.3 Change an existing one — expect 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "CANNOT", "reason": "Changed my mind"}

### 6.4 Delete one — expect 409
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences/2

### 6.5 The schedule itself is still hidden — expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1


### ===========================================================
### 7 — MANUAL ASSIGNMENT (status DRAFT)
### ===========================================================

### 7.0 Back to the manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123"}

### 7.1 Coverage before assigning — every shift short of staff
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/coverage

### 7.2 Who can work shift 1 — expect the full list
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shifts/1/available-employees

### 7.3 Support agents only — expect the list filtered
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shifts/1/available-employees?jobPositionId=2

### 7.4 Who can work shift 2 — Maya shows needsOverrideFor
###     "Marked as unavailable" from 3.10.1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shifts/2/available-employees

### 7.5 Assign Maya to shift 1 — expect 201, no warnings
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 1, "employeeId": 3, "override": false}

### 7.6 The same again — expect 409, already assigned
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 1, "employeeId": 3, "override": false}


### ----- 7.7 OVERRIDABLE: LEAVE -----

### 7.7.1 Assign Omer to shift 4, a day he is on leave
###       expect 409, overridable EMPLOYEE_ON_LEAVE with a consequence
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 4, "employeeId": 4, "override": false}

### 7.7.2 Confirmed — expect 201, overridesApplied names the removed day
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 4, "employeeId": 4, "override": true}

### 7.7.3 The leave now covers 11-12 Aug only — expect one range of 2 days
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves


### ----- 7.8 BLOCKING: REST PERIOD -----

### 7.8.1 Assign Eitan to shift 3, the night of 9 Aug — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 3, "employeeId": 6, "override": false}

### 7.8.2 And to shift 4, the morning right after
###       expect 409, blocking REST_PERIOD, empty overridable
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 4, "employeeId": 6, "override": false}

### 7.8.3 The same with override — still 409
###       A blocking rule cannot be bypassed
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 4, "employeeId": 6, "override": true}


### ----- 7.9 OVERRIDABLE: NO OPEN SLOT -----

### 7.9.1 Assign a senior agent to shift 3, which requires none
###       expect 409, overridable NO_MATCHING_REQUIREMENT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 3, "employeeId": 8, "override": false}

### 7.9.2 Confirmed — expect 201 with override true on the assignment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 3, "employeeId": 8, "override": true}


### ----- 7.10 OVERRIDABLE: CONTRACTED HOURS -----
### Noa is contracted for 24h, three 8-hour shifts.

### 7.10.1 First shift — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 7, "employeeId": 7, "override": false}

### 7.10.2 Second — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 10, "employeeId": 7, "override": false}

### 7.10.3 Third, now at 24h — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 13, "employeeId": 7, "override": false}

### 7.10.4 Fourth would take her to 32h
###        expect 409, overridable MAX_WEEKLY_HOURS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 16, "employeeId": 7, "override": false}

### 7.10.5 Confirmed as overtime — expect 201
###        overridesApplied is empty: nothing was changed, only allowed
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 16, "employeeId": 7, "override": true}


