Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 1, "employeeId": 3, "override": false}


### ===========================================================
### 8 — PUBLISHING (DRAFT -> PUBLISHED)
### ===========================================================

### 8.1 Read the current version before publishing
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1

### 8.2 Publish with a stale version — expect 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0}

### 8.3 Publish with the version from 8.1 — expect 200, status PUBLISHED
###     Replace the number below with what 8.1 returned
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 20}

### 8.4 Publish again — expect 409, no longer DRAFT
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 21}

### 8.5 Edit requirements after publishing — expect 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/shifts/1/requirements
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 21, "requirements": [{"jobPositionId": 2, "requiredCount": 5}]}

### 8.6 Clear assignments after publishing — expect 409
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/1/assignments

### 8.7 A manager may still cover a sick employee — expect 201
###     Manual assignment stays open after publishing
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"shiftId": 2, "employeeId": 9, "override": false}

### 8.8 And remove one — expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/assignments/1


